    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/academics/our-faculty": {
      "title": "Professor Katharine Croce on The Behavioral Observations Podcast",
      "description": "Our Faculty | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Our Faculty More in this section Academics The Holy Family Experience BLUEprint for Student Success Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study School of Arts & Sciences School of Business & Technology School of Education School of Nursing Honors Program Honors Coursework Honors Program Students Honors Program Application Honor Societies at Holy Family Course Catalogs Archive Registrar Registration Information Academic Calendar 2026 - 2027 Winterim Academic Forms Veterans' Affairs Programs Transcripts & Replacement Diplomas Academic Support Services Academic Advising Tiger Tutoring Office for Academic Success Career Development Services Career Resources Signature Programming Series Employer Resources Services Internship Opportunities First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Faculty Senate Library Using the Library Library Catalog Print Books Research Databases Publication Finder Library Instruction Interlibrary Loan Course Reserves Citation Guides Meet Our Faculty Holy Family University faculty are renowned for their expertise in teaching, research, and professional practice. Our professors go beyond academic qualifications to create an open, caring, and supportive learning environment. They are deeply committed to ensuring your success by understanding your unique learning style. Students consistently report that the dedication of our faculty is what makes a Holy Family education not only valuable but truly special. Holy Family University is comprised of four Schools of Study, each with a unique mission. The School of Arts & Sciences provides the liberal arts core of a Holy Family education. Meet the faculty . The School of Business & Technology prepares students for success in the local and global marketplace. Meet the faculty . The School of Education is widely regarded for its academic excellence and commitment to addressing critical societal needs. Meet the faculty . The School of Nursing offers an innovative, cutting-edge education that trains professionals in patient-centered care. Meet the faculty . A Supportive Community Here, family truly is our middle name. At Holy Family University, you'll be mentored by engaged and inspiring professors—respected experts who have the time and commitment to care about your future. You’ll be encouraged to participate in a team setting that mirrors the realities of today’s fast-paced, innovative work environments. You might even choose to travel with a professor in one of our study-abroad programs. Our Academic Philosophy Our commitment to education is shaped by our core values : Family , Respect , Integrity , Service and Responsibility , and Learning . Rooted in our Catholic intellectual tradition, our distinctive core curriculum connects these values with workforce-ready and transferable skills. Through a tiered approach, we ensure you graduate not only with expertise in your field but with essential skills like communication, problem-solving, and ethical decision-making. Our faculty are your guides on this journey. They provide mentorship and hands-on experiences through collaborative research, internships, and service-learning opportunities, preparing you to lead with purpose in your career and in service to your community. At Holy Family, you'll find a true sense of belonging in a vibrant campus community. In The News Dr. Marina Boykova Inducted as Distinguished Fellow Dr. Marina Boykova, an associate professor at Holy Family University, was recently inducted as a Distinguished Fellow in the Nursing Academy of the National Academies of Practice (NAP). Read About the Honor Holy Family University Honors 2025 Taylor Award Recipients Holy Family University is proud to announce the recipients of the 2025 Ray and Mildred Taylor Awards, which will fund six innovative and impactful research projects led by seven distinguished faculty members. Read More About the Award The Hills are Alive…With the Sound of Psychology During Dr. Jill Swirsky’s Psychology of Musical Theater class at Holy Family University, students aren’t just watching beloved films — they’re engaging in deep psychological analysis. Read About the Course Professor Katharine Croce on The Behavioral Observations Podcast Dr. Katharine (Katie) Croce, associate professor at Holy Family University, recently sat down on The Behavioral Observations Podcast to talk about her journey. Read More About the Podcast A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
